// Orbiting, on the right button.
//
// Yaw and pitch in millidegrees, 500 per pixel: a 360-degree turn is 720 pixels
// of travel, about a screen's width, and that is the rate that feels like turning
// an object rather than flinging it.
//
// Dragging right turns the scene right, which means the *camera* goes the other
// way -- hence the minus. Getting this backwards is not subtle to use and is very
// easy to write: the eye orbits opposite to the thing it is looking at.

ed_turn() {
  lset((import ed_st), 2, (import ed_st)[2] - (inp_mx() - (import ed_st)[6]) * 500);
  ed_pitch();
} return void;
